  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "The domain of the vector-valued function $f(t)=(1-{t}^{3})\\,i+3\\operatorname{tan}\u2061t\\,j+\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+1}\\,k$ is \n\n$$\nt\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\\,t\\ne .\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression? You may assume that $n$ is an integer.",
  "worked_solution": "To find the domain of $f$, we need the intersection of the domains of the individual components.\n\n- The domain of the 1st component $1-{t}^{3}$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\n- The domain of the 2nd component $3\\operatorname{tan}\u2061t$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )$, $t\\ne \\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi ,$ where $n$ is an integer.\n\n- The domain of the 3rd component $\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+1}$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nTherefore, the domain of the vector-valued function $f(t)$ is \n\n$$\nt\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\\,t\\ne \\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi ,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer.",
